  "_comment": "The 25 launch metros, defined by COUNTY. County matching is far more accurate than city-name matching: a metro contains hundreds of city names but a manageable list of counties, and the federal hospice dataset includes a county field. Counties are stored uppercase without the word COUNTY - the ingest script normalizes both sides before comparing.",
  "_review_note": "County lists were assembled from CBSA definitions and should be treated as v1. The ingest script prints a coverage report showing high-hospice-count counties in our states that did NOT match any metro - review that output and add anything obviously missing.",
  "_priority_key": {
    "1": "Build first. Home field or unusually dense supply.",
    "2": "Build second. Strong supply signals.",
    "3": "Build third. Large population, supply unproven."
